============================================================================================
GATE SELF-CONTROL
============================================================================================
  must REJECT round 31's rows                 : REJECTED (3 bad pairs)
  must ACCEPT a distinct-latent row set       : ACCEPTED
  must ACCEPT a shared-VALUE non-recoverable  : ACCEPTED
  implementations diffed (runA vs runB)       : 16 calls, 0 disagreements

  ROUND 31's THREE A ROWS FAIL THIS GATE ON ALL THREE PAIRS. Had it existed, the
  build would have refused before dispatch, and the 1/36 that cert_w61_r32 SS8 was
  written around would never have been available to write around.

  SCOPE, because overstating a new gate is how the last four got written:
   * DB is NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT. It tests one shared-latent family -- the
     residue, because that is the identity the brief prints. A brief printing a
     DIFFERENT identity creates a different latent, and this gate will not see it.
   * The latent list must be REBUILT PER BRIEF from the identities that brief
     prints. Hard-coding 'residue' into the line's build scripts would reproduce
     RULING CZ exactly: a check measuring the dimension its fault set came from.
   * It says nothing about GUESSABILITY. Three rows with distinct latents can each
     still have a 3-element plausible set. DB and the null are separate conditions
     and BOTH must be computed before any conjunction is cited.
  elapsed 0.0s

============================================================================================
RIDER -- IS RULING DB EVEN SATISFIABLE ON THIS FAMILY?  (bounded census)
============================================================================================
  population: every partition of 4..34 with >=2 parts whose M terminates
  terminating lists: 36513
  residue histogram: {2: 1741, 3: 7587, 4: 8632, 5: 6647, 6: 4505, 7: 2902, 8: 1824, 9: 1125, 10: 678, 11: 398, 12: 227, 13: 125, 14: 66, 15: 33, 16: 15, 17: 6, 18: 2}
  MODAL RESIDUE 4 covers 8632/36513 = 23.6% of the whole population.
  distinct residue values available at all: 17

  SECOND CUT -- restricted to HAND-COMPUTABLE rows, which is what round 31
  actually required (A rows are 'derivable by hand from section 1 alone'):
    |M| <= 10  :   130 rows,  4 distinct residues, MODAL residue 3 =  50.8%
    |M| <= 12  :   521 rows,  5 distinct residues, MODAL residue 3 =  52.8%
    |M| <= 14  :  2017 rows,  6 distinct residues, MODAL residue 3 =  52.4%
    |M| <= 18  : 12509 rows,  8 distinct residues, MODAL residue 3 =  35.8%

  THE FINDING, AND IT IS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT I EXPECTED WHEN I WROTE THIS RIDER.
  I predicted the residue latent would be near-constant across the family, which
  would have made RULING DB unsatisfiable here. THE CENSUS REFUTES THAT: over the
  full population the residue takes 17 distinct values and the mode holds only
  23.6%. The prediction was wrong and the table above is the authority.

  What the two cuts together actually show is sharper and worse:
   * DB IS SATISFIABLE on this family. Independent rows exist in quantity.
   * The collinearity was manufactured by the HAND-COMPUTABILITY CONSTRAINT.
     Round 31 required its A rows to be derivable by hand, which forces short
     lists, and short lists CONCENTRATE: 4 residue values at |M|<=10 against 17
     over the family, with the top one at 50.8%. Said exactly, because the table
     above is the authority: that modal value is 3, NOT the 2 round 31 drew. So
     the collinearity is BOTH the structural concentration AND an unlucky draw
     inside it -- round 31 landed three rows on a SUB-modal value. Either alone
     would have been survivable; the brief's own hand-derivability rule plus one
     unexamined draw is what collapsed three rows onto one latent.
   * SO THE REPAIR IS NOT 'PICK BETTER SMALL ROWS'. It is that a row set cannot
     be simultaneously hand-derivable AND latent-independent AND numerous on
     this family. Any two of the three. A future brief must choose which to
     drop and say which, before dispatch, in writing.
   * RULING DB must therefore run AFTER the hand-computability filter, never
     before it -- otherwise it certifies a pool the brief will never draw from.
  elapsed 1.7s
